1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:01,210
What's this for?

2
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:03,980
Just because. How's the baby?

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,270
Fast asleep.

4
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:09,250
I'm sorry I missed him. I had to work late.

5
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:11,730
What are the flowers for, Richard?

6
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:16,060
Five years of happiness. Happy anniversary.

7
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:17,950
But our anniversary isn't until Saturday.

8
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:19,260
I couldn't wait.

9
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:23,410
Besides, we are not going to be here Saturday.

10
00:00:23,410 --> 00:00:24,340
We're not?

11
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,850
Uh-uh.

12
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:29,810
Where are we going to be?

13
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:33,460
If you had your choice of all the places in the world.

14
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:37,740
where would you choose to spend our anniversary?

15
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:39,730
The Watermill Inn.

16
00:00:39,730 --> 00:00:42,180
I loved that place when we went on our honeymoon.

17
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:46,280
Perfect! You picked the right place.

18
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:47,640
I don't understand.

19
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,270
You and I, Mrs. Stewart,

20
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:53,410
are going to spend a second honeymoon at the Watermill Inn.

21
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:57,180
Oh, Richard! That's wonderful, but--

22
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:58,380
No buts.

23
00:00:58,380 --> 00:00:59,200
What about the baby?

24
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:00,720
Aren't we taking the baby on our honeymoon?

25
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:01,980
Absolutely not.

26
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:04,160
The world's greatest grandmother, Mrs. Ellen Stewart,

27
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:07,610
has agreed to take care of him for the weekend.

28
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:10,810
Richard, isn't that too much to ask of your mother?

29
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:14,890
Too much? She loves taking care of Max.

30
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:19,470
But ... I'll miss him.

31
00:01:19,470 --> 00:01:21,380
Well, we'll phone every hour,

32
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:24,180
and you can listen to him over the phone.

33
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,670
Come on, Mar.

34
00:01:25,670 --> 00:01:28,700
It's time you and I had a romantic weekend alone together.

35
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:35,850
We've earned it. What do you say?

36
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:38,680
It does sound tempting.

37
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:41,280
You're right. We've earned it.

38
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:46,470
Great! I'll make a reservation right now.

39
00:01:46,470 --> 00:01:47,880
Remember that wonderful little balcony

40
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,650
where we had our meals ...

41
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:52,410
with a view of the Hudson River?

42
00:01:52,410 --> 00:02:03,830
How could I forget?

43
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:06,900
Hello. Is Mrs. Montefiore there?

44
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:09,560
Ah. She's out.

45
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,190
Yes. This is Richard Stewart.

46
00:02:11,190 --> 00:02:15,200
My wife and I spent our honeymoon at the inn.

47
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,920
No, we didn't leave anything in the room.

48
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,230
It's five years ago.

49
00:02:18,230 --> 00:02:21,190
We'd like to make a reservation for this weekend.

50
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:27,520
Yes, a double room, please. What?

51
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:34,800
Are you sure? But ... OK.

52
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,310
Nothing available.

53
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:38,470
Wait! Don't hang up!

54
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:42,950
Can you recommend someplace nice--someplace nearby?

55
00:02:42,950 --> 00:02:53,270
Uh--hold it. Old Country Inn?

56
00:02:53,270 --> 00:02:59,030
Right. And the phone number?

57
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:04,780
555-2420. Thank you. 555-2420

58
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:06,630
He says there's another inn

59
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:10,100
just half a mile down the road from the Watermill.

60
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:13,490
It won't be the same, but what do you say?

61
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:13,970
Well ...

62
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:16,280
My mom is available to baby-sit this weekend.

63
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:19,510
Well, OK. See if they have a room.

64
00:03:19,510 --> 00:03:28,440
Right!

65
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:31,430
Hello. Is this the Old Country Inn?

66
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:32,990
Yes. This is Richard Stewart.

67
00:03:32,990 --> 00:03:35,850
The desk clerk at the Watemill suggested your inn.

68
00:03:35,850 --> 00:03:38,090
Would you happen to have a room for two availbale

69
00:03:38,090 --> 00:03:39,940
this weekend?

70
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:41,240
Something really nice.

71
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:45,320
My wife and I are celebrating our fifth anniversary.

72
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:50,710
Yes. I'll hold. He's checking. You do?

73
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:54,550
Great! What is the daily rate?

74
00:03:54,550 --> 00:03:56,800
That's fine. Thank you.

75
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:01,460
Yes, we'll be arriving by car about ten o'clock Friday night.

76
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:09,530
Stewart. S-t-e-w-a-r-t. Thank you.

77
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:14,090
Done! You and I, Mrs. Stewart.

78
00:04:14,090 --> 00:04:19,280
are going to have a wonderful, romantic weekend!

79
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:22,280
Richard, that's the baby. Richard
